    "created_at": "2015-11-24T09:47:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-24T09:47:17Z",
    "body": "With qualified names you could still have the same string appear multiple times, do we just live with that? It would be nice if one didn't have to resort to `NamedNodeMap` to guarantee that all attributes are found, but I see no other way to give that guarantee than to have a namespace+localName tuple :(\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
